## PHASE 7 — Final Verdict Message

After writing the file and updating control.md, print the verdict:

If `DO NOT MERGE`:
> "🚨 **DO NOT MERGE** — Critical risks found. Resolve all 🔴 Critical items in `ai-dev/<ticket-number>/impact.md` and run `/impact <ticket-number>` again to re-evaluate."

If `LOW`:
> "⚠️ **Merge confidence LOW** — High-risk issues need attention before this is safe to merge. See `ai-dev/<ticket-number>/impact.md` for the Pre-Merge Checklist."

If `MEDIUM`:
> "🟡 **Merge confidence MEDIUM** — No critical blockers. Review the High Risk items and Pre-Merge Checklist in `ai-dev/<ticket-number>/impact.md` before raising the PR."

If `HIGH`:
> "✅ **Merge confidence HIGH** — No significant risks found. Full report in `ai-dev/<ticket-number>/impact.md`. You're good to raise a PR."

---

## Merge Confidence Scoring Logic

| Condition | Confidence |
|---|---|
| Any Critical risk found | `DO NOT MERGE` |
| 3+ High risks found | `LOW` |
| 1–2 High risks OR 3+ Medium risks | `MEDIUM` |
| Only Low/Informational findings | `HIGH` |

---

## Error Handling

- If branch has no commits vs develop: "No changes detected. This branch is identical to develop."
- If `git diff` is very large (100+ files): analyse the highest-classification files first, note that others were spot-checked
- If no `src/` directory found: adapt paths to whatever source directory exists in the project root
- If TypeScript is not used: skip Pass 6 silently
